# The working tree of this plugin must be byte-identical to what is committed.
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF blobs to CRLF on checkout, and git then
# reports the result as clean because it normalises line endings when it compares. The rewrite is
# invisible to `git status` while it is happening.
#
# That matters more here than in most plugins: `miniapp/node/vendor/dynamic-workflows/` is an
# unmodified copy of the upstream 0.8.2 runtime, and its own LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt
# say the files are redistributed as-is. `text=auto` leaves git free to keep deciding for itself
# which files are binary; `eol=lf` is the part that pins the result. Every blob here is already
# LF, so adding this changes no committed content — it only stops the working tree from
# disagreeing with it.
#
# This file lives in the plugin directory, not the repository root. At the root it would rewrite
# line endings for every other plugin in the repository, and this is a single-plugin change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The files in this plugin that are not text.
*.png binary
*.wasm binary
